r VTEC  turbo engine with direct fuel injection  it has 235 kilowatts of power and goes  from 0 to 100 kilometers an hour and 5.7  seconds its top speed is 272 Michele  says the acceleration is amazing  although she's a novice on the test  track the car makes her feel assured so  she's confident enough to put the hammer  down in defiance again the new Type R  has three driving modes in addition to  comfort and sport there is our plus in  that mode the handling and throttle are  more direct the gears are more powerful  and the car is more agile for everyday  driving the comfort mode is better the  Honda Civic Type R is built to appeal  not just to amateur car racers but the  families as well Michelle says that the  car takes a bit of getting used to in  this respect but the vehicle offers the  driver lots of support it holds curves  and she can hit the gas whenever she  wants and the car doesn't let her down  Lucinda on the gas game on the  Evangelist and furnishing station the  interior has been completely redone and  there are marked improvements in quality  comfort and workmanship when you get  into the car you spot the red and black  sporty seats right away Honda has  lowered those seats by 5 centimeters  speed is displayed digitally in the  center of the tachometer the cockpit is  well designed on the drivers right-hand  side there's the gearshift for the  manual 6-speed transmission the  seven-inch touchscreen in the center  console has replaced a whole bunch of  buttons  [Applause]  Honda is proud of setting a record on  the Nurburgring demanding Nordschleife  of course for the lap time of seven  minutes and forty three point eight  seconds the type R is the fastest  front-wheel drive car ever as a show  says her test lap was really fun she's  still full of adrenaline and her hands  and knees are shaking but she says that  the Honda Civic Type R was a pleasant  surprise  and she had a really great day with it  even resolve our car test three Manuel  Schaefer says smarts new IDI or electric  drive convertible aims to be as clean as  the water from this spring the current  generation fortwo Cabrio has been on the  market since 2016 the new generation  smart electric drive came out just a few  months ago now Smart has combined the  two the Cabrio comes with the same 60  kilowatt electric motor that powers the  regular four to IDI to improve its range  top speed is electronically limited to  130 kilometers per hour  [Music]  a man was driving a convertible is great  though waiting at traffic lights in the  city and breathing in the exhaust from  the other cars isn't so nice so it's  good that due to its 150 kilometer plus  range you can also drive this kibriya  out into the countryside being  surrounded by green makes for a truly  green driving experience  the battery pack located in the  underbody has a capacity of seventeen  point six kilowatt hours a 22 kilowatt  onboard charger with fast charge  functionality is due out in Europe next  spring it should allow the battery to  charge to 80 percent in less than 45  minutes smarts project of Illinois  coordinator calls the Cabrillo a dream  car and the perfect city car it fits in  every parking space and as a tiny  turning radius like the regular smarts  with internal combustion engines but  with the electric drive there's the  added advantage that when driving around  with the top down we get to hear what's  going on around us we hear the birds  pedestrians other cars that's a unique  feeling that only an electric  convertible can deliver  I mean Escovedo meeting Connor on the  outside the electric drive Cabrillo  looks much the same as Smart's fuel  powered models potential buyers can find  out which version they're looking at by  reading the name on the emblems the  optional Braavos design package gives  the convertible a sporty look  the IDI logo which looks like a plug in  an electric socket figures prominently  at the side the soft top can be opened  up electronically but the roof bars have  to be removed by hand and then stored in  their designated place in the trunk that  reduces cargo space from 340 to 260  liters the Braavos tailor-made exterior  style package includes accents supplied  by the high performance tuning company  as well as LED tail lights the interior  is simple and uncluttered colorful  accents which match the paint job at a  bit of Pettit the display in the  speedometer shows the remaining range in  current speed a free-standing dial  provides data on the charging status and  the battery pack  like all the other four to models the  electric drive convertible has a tiny  turning radius of less than seven meters  together whether it's green Creed this  makes it an ideal city car smart is now  taking orders for the new fortwo Cabrio  electric drive prices started just over  25 thousand euros in Germany here  financial incentives are being offered  to get more electric cars on the road so  the real cost is less than 21 thousand  euros Kumanovo says for him Smart's  electric drive Cabrio has it all it  combines all the strengths of its fellow  smarts the compact external dimensions  the convertible experience and on top of  that its emissions free you could say  it's three cars in one  five becomes six this autumn BMW will  unveil the 6 Series Gran Turismo the  successor to the 5 Series GT the 6  Series GT looks more like a coupe a than  a sedan several engine options will be  available including the four-cylinder  gas-powered 630i  that generates 190 kilowatts and 400  Newton meters of torque it's been  carried over from the five series  six-cylinder diesel and gas powered  engines will also be on offer the latest  addition to the successful Skoda Octavia  line is the Rs 245 it's the fastest  Octavia ever with a 180 kilowatt engine  that's 11 kilowatts more than the RS 232  245 can jump from 0 to 100 km/h in 6.6  seconds and features a sport chassis  that's 15 millimeters lower than its  previous models German prices for the  sedan start at about 34 thousand euros  and 35 thousand for the station wagon  our s about e these two letters stand  for high-performance cars but they can  top them too we're testing out the Audi  rs6 Avant performance  it's got thirty-three kilowatts more  power than the standard rs6 Avant car  tester and elite Zimmerman says that the  best thing about the rs6 performance is  definitely the motor a four liter v8  with two turbochargers that puts out 445  kilowatts and an amazing 750 Newton  meters of torque that makes the rs6  performance one of the fastest station  wagons in the world the car goes from 0  to 100 kilometers an hour and just 3.7  seconds that's 0.2 seconds faster than  the basic rs6 model some people might  not like the rs6 Avant performances fuel  consumption and co2 emissions but this  vehicle is not designed to protect the  environment  these are mojo Andre says that the motor  grabs your attention with its beautiful  sound especially in leave dynamic mode  dynamic models  even when standing still this model rs6  projects Authority the chassis is about  six centimetres wider than the standard  a6  the tires are 275 millimeters wide on 20  inch rims extra length at the front and  especially the back are typical of this  series  [Music]  the powerful motor which is mounted in  front of the front axle is connected to  a classic Quattro Drive this layout  means that the car as a whole is front  weighted which affects its handling  [Music]  Hondo he says that although the rs6  sDrive is weighted more to the back  which means more torque is distributed  there this car is better suited to long  extrude stretches of Autobahn and long  curves than to tight curves which it  takes primarily with its front wheels  still you definitely feel safe an rs6  rapidly approaching in your rear-view  mirror is an imposing sight and there's  a dynamic plus option which costs an  additional 14 thousand euros and takes  the cars top speed at 305 kilometers an  hour  [Music]  the interior harkens back to the roots  of the Audi a6  but lots of carbon fiber trim RS logos  and the flat-bottom steering wheel still  give it a sporty feel the start button  is fiery red the honeycomb leather seats  are standard  [Music]  MIT family Andre says that the rs6  performance is not a sensible car but  people who can afford it will find that  this car will perform well in almost any  situation and besides not being sensible  can be a lot of fun like on the rs6 is a  station wagon of extremes  extremely fast extremely powerful  extremely exclusive and extremely  expensive  [Music]  what was stuffy a big country car  Chester honey let's Texas Volvo is known  for building robust cars like the second  generation of the xc90 it's in the top  class of SUVs the first generation Volvo  xc90 first hit the market in 2002  Volvo's stuck with a design for 13 years  that didn't go down well with some  dealers who prefer to see models change  every six or seven years so Volvo came  out with the second generation as  competition for the BMW x5 and Audi q7  honey points out that this xc90 is  powered by a four-cylinder engine with a  capacity of 2 liters various performance  and fuel options are available there's  even a plug-in hybrid but he thinks a  car this big should really have a v6  engine the family studies a POSIX clan  chorus the ultimate role of wood but  does the smaller engine mean that the  xc90 somehow has less to offer we're  going to test the d5 AWD model which  features four-wheel drive  [Music]  the Volvo our design gives this car a  performance inspired look and feel with  the enhanced Polestar version of the  engine the xc90 can jump from 0 to 100  km/h in 7.7 seconds and hit a top speed  of 220 kilometers an hour  rami says that this xc90 has been  outfitted with pole star performance  optimizing software which boosts engine  power by a whopping 4 kilowatts it costs  an extra 1200 euros but it's good value  for money the software not only boost  power but also torque to 500 Newton  meters instead of 480 you can really  feel the difference 1500 rpms can sure  get this 2 ton vehicle moving months  enough on our test car was painted  Sweden blue other options besides color  include 22 inch rims this version of the  xc90  is 15 centimeters longer than the  previous version and 2 centimetres wider  Ronnie says the car's interior is really  comfortable everything is where it's  supposed to be nice and tidy the  controls are all here on the big  touchscreen he thinks it all looks great  but it's a little awkward at first until  you figure out where everything is there  are more apps here than Ronnie has on  his phone and if you don't find the  heater app quickly you'll either freeze  or roast it maybe quibbling but he'd  still rather have a few proper push  buttons okay it's making a whole new  board as much as Michaan's refurbished  Ronnie really likes the Bowers &amp; Wilkins  sound system whether it's 1,400 watts  and 20 speakers keynotes all interstate  the interior is quite posh there's  carbon fiber trim stainless steel and  leather everywhere you look  a 24 centimeter touchpad allows you to  control just about everything except the  basics there's lots of room in here too  even with five passengers and there's an  add-on option for a third row of seats  [Music]  mommy says that this model with the d5  diesel engine the our design features  Pulstar optimization and a few other  extras will cost around ninety thousand  euros this car has a lot to offer a  powerful engine a streamlined chassis  and a world-class sound system and the  seats are really comfortable  Futaba vino Ronnie says the Volvo xc90  is a first-class car and he can't wait  to see what Volvo comes up with next  [Music]  our classic car expert Christophe Bauer  is tooling around the northern Italian  province of Trentino in a Porsche on the  virtually empty roads of the plateau of  lava ani he finds it hard not to fall in  love with a 911 Targa deposit line  christophe says the Porsche 911 is the  sports car park Salons now as ever  its shape is immediately recognizable  here targis stands for the removable  roof which normally sits between the  windshield and the roll bar the Targa's  roll bar was the brainchild of company  chairman ferry Porsche and his son  Ferdinand Alexander Porsche who designed  the 911 the roll bar was made to protect  the convertibles inhabitants in case the  car flipped over  but its appearance drew mixed reactions  some even joke the targets brush tanner  hasta Steel rhobar reminded them of pots  and pans and had them reaching for their  dishcloths  still over a quarter of the 911s  produced at the time were targets  [Applause]  unfocus that christophe says that at  first the targa was a quick fix the US  was Porsches biggest market then and  still is today but in the 1960s an  ambitious lawyer named Ralph Nader  launched his unsafe at any speed crusade  to get dangerous cars off the roads  especially convertibles so Porsche  quickly developed a safe convertible  with a roll bar and the Targa was born  Christoph feels the name was well chosen  it harks back to the Targa Florio  endurance races held on Sicily and Targa  is an old word for shield clever huh the  Targa has been rolling off assembly line  since 1965 unlike its predecessor the  356 which had always been available as a  convertible the 911 only came as a coupe  a when the model was first introduced in  1963 knowin that knowing on things tough  tells us Porsche started fitting the  target with panoramic glass rear windows  in 1969 before that there was a plastic  one that zipped open the problem was you  often couldn't shut it again as the  plastic shrunk at low temperatures he  says this 1972 model has a different  weak spot to achieve better weight  distribution the oil tank was mounted  just ahead of the rear axle and filled  here you can guess what happened some  owners or gas station attendants filled  it with gas causing major engine damage  just a year later the oil tank lid was  history  it's harmonious shape has made the  portion 9/11 one of the world's most  beautiful and timeless sports cars the  target roll bar and the wraparound rear  window continue the flowing lines seen  at the front with its centrally placed  tachometer wings that are visible from  the driver's seat and ignition to the  left of the steering wheel the targa  boasts all the classic features of a 911  not to mention its rear engine a Porsche  trademark  [Applause]  this 911 T was the weakest variant of  the 6-cylinder 2.4 liter engine which  was fitted into the models starting in  1972  Christophe says these days 130  horsepower sounds more suitable for a  family car than a racy sports car but  not here as this is a porsche after all  the engine revs willingly and  accelerates quickly going from zero to  100 kilometres an hour in just 10  seconds and it can hit 200 km/h so you  can still drive it with confidence today  even the highway police appreciated the  cars combination of fresh air and  driving performance the hundred  thousandth Porsche ever made was a 912  Targa  equipped with a blue light for the  German police  [Music]  as a Cristo says fans swear the 911s  handling is second to none the rear  engine delivers endless amounts of  traction making frills like power  steering and ESP superfluous he calls it  the perfect recipe for endless driving  pleasure but compared to modern 911s  cornering stability is limited so when  you enter a curve quickly and suddenly  take your foot off the gas the rear end  can slide out then you must quickly  counter steer to get back on track  what's the biggie but such driving  challenges and the inimitable throaty  sound of the air-cooled boxer engine are  the ingredients that have made the  classic 911 such a success story  [Music]  then whenever Christoph says the 911 is  the most successful supercar of all time  like no other it balances sportiness  with everyday practicality and with the  911 target Porsche added a trend-setting  security concept  he says the cars the perfect synthesis  of hedonism and rationality of open-air  feeling and safety and that makes the  911 Targa a true milestone and  automotive history in 1982 another  Porsche started to give the Targa a run  for its money the 911 convertible after  a 16-year break the sports car maker  returned to making open top vehicles  without roll bars still the Targa  remains and Porsches lineup to this day  and next time on drive it a great city  runabout with new details the Skoda  Citigo and putting the Jaguar F peace  through its paces  [Music]  [Music]

